  "text": "I am writing to express my extreme frustration with my recent purchase experience. As a first-time buyer, I expected a smooth transaction, but I was completely blindsided when my credit card was declined. I was trying to purchase a high-end mountain bike and a full set of camping gear, which totaled $5,200.00. I understand that your maximum credit card transaction limit is $5,000.00, but this rigid cutoff is incredibly inconvenient and feels like a trap for customers who are just trying to equip themselves for a trip. I am not asking for a discount or a special price; I am simply asking if there is any way you can process this single transaction despite the $5,000.00 limit. Splitting the payment into two separate transactions feels like a hassle that shouldn't be necessary for a legitimate purchase. I have already spent hours researching and selecting these items, and I do not want to have to return them or find another retailer because of an arbitrary financial cap. Please let me know if there is any flexibility in this situation so I can complete my order without further delay or stress."
